#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:210
msgid "Interactivity Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:212
msgid "Keep JS minimal. Common patterns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:214
msgid "**Tab switching:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:215
msgid ""
"document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab]').forEach(tab => {\n"
"    tab.addEventListener('click', () => {\n"
"        document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab]').forEach(t => "
"t.classList.remove('active'));\n"
"        document.querySelectorAll('[data-panel]').forEach(p => "
"p.style.display = 'none');\n"
"        tab.classList.add('active');\n"
"        document.querySelector(`[data-"
"panel=\"${tab.dataset.tab}\"]`).style.display = 'block';\n"
"    });\n"
"});\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:226
msgid "**Modal toggle:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:227
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"function toggleModal(id) {\n"
"    const modal = document.getElementById(id);\n"
"    modal.style.display = modal.style.display === 'flex' ? 'none' : "
"'flex';\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:234
msgid "**Dropdown:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:235
msgid ""
"function toggleDropdown(id) {\n"
"    const dd = document.getElementById(id);\n"
"    dd.style.display = dd.style.display === 'block' ? 'none' : 'block';\n"
"}\n"
"document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n"
"    if (!e.target.closest('.dropdown')) {\n"
"        document.querySelectorAll('.dropdown-menu').forEach(d => "
"d.style.display = 'none');\n"
"    }\n"
"});\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:247
msgid "Realistic Data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:249
msgid "Use realistic-looking placeholder data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:251
msgid ""
"Names: \"Sarah Chen\", \"Marcus Johnson\", \"Aisha Patel\" (diverse, "
"realistic)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:252
msgid "Emails: \"sarah.chen@example.com\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:253
msgid "Dates: Use relative dates (\"2 hours ago\", \"Yesterday\", \"Mar 15\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:254
msgid ""
"Numbers: Use realistic ranges (not round numbers — \"$12,847\" not "
"\"$10,000\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:255
msgid "Status values: Use the actual statuses from the spec if available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:257
msgid "What NOT to Do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:259
msgid "Don't use CDN links or external resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:260
msgid "Don't use Lorem Ipsum — write realistic placeholder text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:261
msgid ""
"Don't use icon fonts — use simple inline SVG or Unicode characters (▶ ● ✓"
" ✕ ⋯ ↓ →)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:262
msgid "Don't add complex animations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:263
msgid "Don't use canvas or WebGL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:264
msgid ""
"Don't make it pixel-perfect — it's a prototype for discussion, not "
"production code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:265
msgid "Don't include more than 2-3 screens in one file — keep it focused"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:267
msgid "Spec write-back"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:269
msgid ""
"When invoked against a spec slug (not free-text), after saving the "
"mockup, link it back from the originating spec so delivery agents can "
"find it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:271
msgid "Locate the spec. Try in order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:272
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`.hero/planning/features/{slug}/spec.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:273
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`.hero/planning/bugs/{slug}/spec.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:274
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`.hero/specs/{slug}/spec.md` (archive fallback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:275
msgid ""
"If a `## Mockups` section does not exist, append one near the end of the "
"spec body. Place it before `## Validation` if that section exists; "
"otherwise at the end of the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:276
msgid "Add an entry in this format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:278
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"- [{Mockup name}](.hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html) — YYYY-MM-DD — one-line "
"description of what the mockup shows\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:282
msgid ""
"Default the name to a humanized slug (e.g. `Hero landing page`). Use "
"something more specific when the spec has multiple mockups or iteration "
"variants (e.g. `Hero landing page — dense variant`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:283
msgid "Use today's date in ISO format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:284
msgid "Keep the description to one line — what's shown, not why."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:286
msgid "Iteration semantics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:288
msgid ""
"On `--iterate`, match the existing entry by path. If the path is "
"unchanged (the common case — overwriting `index.html`), update the date "
"in place and rewrite the description only if the iteration meaningfully "
"changed what's depicted. Don't append a duplicate row. If the iteration "
"produces a new file (e.g. `dense.html` alongside `index.html`), append a "
"new entry instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:290
msgid "Free-text exception"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/html-mockup-generation/SKILL.md:292
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When `/mock` is invoked with free-text rather than a spec slug, there is "
"no spec to write back to. Save the mockup under `.hero/mocks/_adhoc"
"/{kebab-case-summary}/index.html` and skip the write-back step entirely. "
"This keeps the `.hero/mocks/` root clean — slug-keyed dirs match real "
"specs; `_adhoc/` clearly doesn't."
msgstr ""

